(window.IND_GITA_V = window.IND_GITA_V || {})[9] = [{"v":1,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":"श्री भगवानुवाच","spp":"before","sa":"इदं तु ते गुह्यतमं प्रवक्ष्याम्यनसूयवे ।\nज्ञानं विज्ञानसहितं यज्ज्ञात्वा मोक्ष्यसेऽशुभात् ॥","iast":"idaṃ tu te guhyatamaṃ pravakṣyāmyanasūyave |\njñānaṃ vijñānasahitaṃ yajjñātvā mokṣyase’śubhāt ||","read":"idam tu te guhyatamam pravakshyaamyanasooyave |\njnaanam vijnaanasahitam yajjnaatvaa mokshyase'shubhaat ||","spli":"śrī bhagavānuvāca","splr":"shree bhagavaanuvaacha","en":"The Blessed Lord said: To thee, the uncarping, verily shall I declare this profoundest Secret, wisdom with knowledge combined, which, having known, thou shalt be freed from evil.","en2":"To thee, who dost not carp, verily shall I now declare this, the most profound knowledge, united with realisation, having known which, thou shalt be free from evil (Samsâra).","en2r":null,"rv":null,"kid":"Krishna tells Arjuna, who does not find fault, that he will now share the deepest secret knowledge. When Arjuna knows it, he will be set free from evil."},{"v":2,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"राजविद्या राजगुह्यं पवित्रमिदमुत्तमम् ।\nप्रत्यक्षावगमं धर्म्यं सुसुखं कर्तुमव्ययम् ॥","iast":"rājavidyā rājaguhyaṃ pavitramidamuttamam |\npratyakṣāvagamaṃ dharmyaṃ susukhaṃ kartumavyayam ||","read":"raajavidyaa raajaguhyam pavitramidamuttamam |\npratyakshaavagamam dharmyam susukham kartumavyayam ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"Kingly Science, kingly Secret, supreme Purifier, this; intuitional, according to righteousness, very easy to perform, imperishable.","en2":"Of sciences, the highest; of profundities, the deepest; of purifiers, the supreme, is this; realisable by direct perception, endowed with (immense) merit, very easy to perform, and of an imperishable nature.","en2r":null,"rv":null,"kid":"Krishna says this knowledge is the highest, the deepest secret and the greatest purifier. It can be known directly, it is good, it is very easy to practise, and it never perishes."},{"v":3,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"अश्रद्दधानाः पुरुषा धर्मस्यास्य परन्तप ।\nअप्राप्य मां निवर्तन्ते मृत्युसंसारवर्त्मनि ॥","iast":"aśraddadhānāḥ puruṣā dharmasyāsya parantapa |\naprāpya māṃ nivartante mṛtyusaṃsāravartmani ||","read":"ashraddadhaanaah purushaa dharmasyaasya parantapa |\napraapya maam nivartante mrityusamsaaravartmani ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"Men without faith in this knowledge, O Parantapa, not reaching Me, return to the paths of this world of death.","en2":"Persons without Shraddhâ for this Dharma, return, O scorcher of foes, without attaining Me, to the path of re-birth fraught with death.","en2r":null,"rv":null,"kid":"Krishna says that people who have no faith in this teaching do not reach him. They come back again to the path of this world, a world of death."},{"v":4,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"मया ततमिदं सर्वं जगदव्यक्तमूर्तिना ।\nमत्स्थानि सर्वभूतानि न चाहं तेष्ववस्थितः ॥","iast":"mayā tatamidaṃ sarvaṃ jagadavyaktamūrtinā |\nmatsthāni sarvabhūtāni na cāhaṃ teṣvavasthitaḥ ||","read":"mayaa tatamidam sarvam jagadavyaktamoortinaa |\nmatsthaani sarvabhootaani na chaaham teshvavasthitah ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"By Me all this world is pervaded in My unmanifested aspect; all beings have root in Me, I am not rooted in them.","en2":"All this world is pervaded by me in My unmanifested form: all beings exist in Me, but I do not dwell in them.","en2r":null,"rv":null,"kid":"Krishna says that, in a form that cannot be seen, he fills this whole world. All beings rest in him, but he does not rest in them."},{"v":5,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"न च मत्स्थानि भूतानि पश्य मे योगमैश्वरम् ।\nभूतभृन्न च भूतस्थो ममात्मा भूतभावनः ॥","iast":"na ca matsthāni bhūtāni paśya me yogamaiśvaram |\nbhūtabhṛnna ca bhūtastho mamātmā bhūtabhāvanaḥ ||","read":"na cha matsthaani bhootaani pashya me yogamaishvaram |\nbhootabhrinna cha bhootastho mamaatmaa bhootabhaavanah ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"Nor have beings root in Me; behold My sovereign Yoga! The support of beings, yet not rooted in beings, My Self their efficient cause.","en2":"Nor do beings exist in Me (in reality), behold My Divine Yoga! Bringing forth and supporting the beings, My Self does not dwell in them.","en2r":null,"rv":null,"kid":"Then Krishna says that beings do not really rest in him either, and asks Arjuna to see his wonderful power. He brings beings forth and holds them up, yet he does not dwell in them."},{"v":6,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"यथाऽऽकाशस्थितो नित्यं वायुः सर्वत्रगो महान् ।\nतथा सर्वाणि भूतानि मत्स्थानीत्युपधारय ॥","iast":"yathā’’kāśasthito nityaṃ vāyuḥ sarvatrago mahān |\ntathā sarvāṇi bhūtāni matsthānītyupadhāraya ||","read":"yathaa''kaashasthito nityam vaayuh sarvatrago mahaan |\ntathaa sarvaani bhootaani matsthaaneetyupadhaaraya ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"As the mighty air everywhere moving is rooted in the Ether, so all beings rest rooted in Me—thus know thou.","en2":"As the mighty wind, moving always everywhere, rests ever in the Akâsha, know thou, that even so do all beings rest in Me.","en2r":null,"rv":null,"kid":"Krishna gives a picture. The mighty wind moves everywhere, yet it always rests in space. In the same way, he says, all beings rest in him."},{"v":7,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"सर्वभूतानि कौन्तेय प्रकृतिं यान्ति मामिकाम् ।\nकल्पक्षये पुनस्तानि कल्पादौ विसृजाम्यहम् ॥","iast":"sarvabhūtāni kaunteya prakṛtiṃ yānti māmikām |\nkalpakṣaye punastāni kalpādau visṛjāmyaham ||","read":"sarvabhootaani kaunteya prakritim yaanti maamikaam |\nkalpakshaye punastaani kalpaadau visrijaamyaham ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"All beings, O Kaunteya, enter my lower nature at the end of a world-age; at the beginning of a world-age again I emanate them.","en2":"At the end of a Kalpa, O son of Kunti, all beings go back to My Prakriti: at the beginning of (another) Kalpa, I send them forth again.","en2r":null,"rv":null,"kid":"Krishna tells Arjuna that at the end of an age of the world, all beings go back into his nature. When a new age begins, he sends them out again."},{"v":8,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"प्रकृतिं स्वामवष्टभ्य विसृजामि पुनः पुनः ।\nभूतग्राममिमं कृत्स्नमवशं प्रकृतेर्वशात् ॥","iast":"prakṛtiṃ svāmavaṣṭabhya visṛjāmi punaḥ punaḥ |\nbhūtagrāmamimaṃ kṛtsnamavaśaṃ prakṛtervaśāt ||","read":"prakritim svaamavashtabhya visrijaami punah punah |\nbhootagraamamimam kritsnamavasham prakritervashaat ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"Hidden in Nature, which is mine own, I emanate again and again all this multitude of beings, helpless, by the force of Nature.","en2":"Animating My Prakriti, I project again and again this whole multitude of beings, helpless under the sway of Prakriti.","en2r":null,"rv":null,"kid":"Krishna says that through his own nature he brings forth all these many beings, again and again. They are helpless, carried along by the power of that nature."},{"v":9,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"न च मां तानि कर्माणि निबध्नन्ति धनञ्जय ।\nउदासीनवदासीनमसक्तं तेषु कर्मसु ॥","iast":"na ca māṃ tāni karmāṇi nibadhnanti dhanañjaya |\nudāsīnavadāsīnamasaktaṃ teṣu karmasu ||","read":"na cha maam taani karmaani nibadhnanti dhananjaya |\nudaaseenavadaaseenamasaktam teshu karmasu ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"Nor do these works bind me, O Dhananjaya, enthroned on high unattached to actions.","en2":"These acts do not bind Me, sitting as one neutral, unattached to them, O Dhananjaya.","en2r":null,"rv":null,"kid":"Krishna tells Arjuna that these works do not bind him. He sits apart from them, like one who takes no side, not attached to what he does."},{"v":10,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"मयाऽध्यक्षेण प्रकृतिः सूयते सचराचरम् ।\nहेतुनाऽनेन कौन्तेय जगद्विपरिवर्तते ॥","iast":"mayā’dhyakṣeṇa prakṛtiḥ sūyate sacarācaram |\nhetunā’nena kaunteya jagadviparivartate ||","read":"mayaa'dhyakshena prakritih sooyate sacharaacharam |\nhetunaa'nena kaunteya jagadviparivartate ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"Under Me as supervisor, Nature sends forth the moving and unmoving: because of this, O Kaunteya, the universe revolves.","en2":"By reason of My proximity, Prakriti produces all this, the moving and the unmoving; the world wheels round and round, O son of Kunti, because of this.","en2r":null,"rv":null,"kid":"Krishna says that with him near, watching over it, nature brings forth everything that moves and everything that does not. Because of this, the world keeps turning."},{"v":11,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"अवजानन्ति मां मूढा मानुषीं तनुमाश्रितम् ।\nपरं भावमजानन्तो मम भूतमहेश्वरम् ॥","iast":"avajānanti māṃ mūḍhā mānuṣīṃ tanumāśritam |\nparaṃ bhāvamajānanto mama bhūtamaheśvaram ||","read":"avajaananti maam moodhaa maanusheem tanumaashritam |\nparam bhaavamajaananto mama bhootamaheshvaram ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"The foolish disregard Me, when clad in human semblance, ignorant of My supreme nature, the great Lord of beings;","en2":"Unaware of My higher state, as the great Lord of beings, fools disregard Me, dwelling in the human form.","en2r":null,"rv":null,"kid":"Krishna says that foolish people look down on him when he comes in a human body. They do not know his higher nature as the great Lord of all beings."},{"v":12,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"मोघाशा मोघकर्माणो मोघज्ञाना विचेतसः ।\nराक्षसीमासुरीं चैव प्रकृतिं मोहिनीं श्रिताः ॥","iast":"moghāśā moghakarmāṇo moghajñānā vicetasaḥ |\nrākṣasīmāsurīṃ caiva prakṛtiṃ mohinīṃ śritāḥ ||","read":"moghaashaa moghakarmaano moghajnaanaa vichetasah |\nraakshaseemaasureem chaiva prakritim mohineem shritaah ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"Empty of hope, empty of deeds, empty of wisdom, senseless, partaking of the deceitful, brutal and demoniacal nature.","en2":"Of vain hopes, of vain works, of vain knowledge, and senseless, they verily are possessed of the delusive nature of Râkshasas and Asuras.","en2r":null,"rv":null,"kid":"Krishna says such people have empty hopes, empty deeds and empty knowledge. They have lost their good sense and take on a cruel, deceiving, demon-like nature."},{"v":13,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"महात्मानस्तु मां पार्थ दैवीं प्रकृतिमाश्रिताः ।\nभजन्त्यनन्यमनसो ज्ञात्वा भूतादिमव्ययम् ॥","iast":"mahātmānastu māṃ pārtha daivīṃ prakṛtimāśritāḥ |\nbhajantyananyamanaso jñātvā bhūtādimavyayam ||","read":"mahaatmaanastu maam paartha daiveem prakritimaashritaah |\nbhajantyananyamanaso jnaatvaa bhootaadimavyayam ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"Verily the Mahâtmâs, O Partha, partaking of My divine nature, worship with unwavering mind, having known Me, the imperishable source of beings.","en2":"But the great-souled ones, O son of Prithâ, possessed of the Divine Prakriti, knowing Me to be the origin of beings, and immutable, worship Me with a single mind.","en2r":null,"rv":null,"kid":"Krishna says the great-souled ones share his divine nature. They know him as the never-ending source of all beings, and they worship him with a mind that never wavers."},{"v":14,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"सततं कीर्तयन्तो मां यतन्तश्च दृढव्रताः ।\nनमस्यन्तश्च मां भक्त्या नित्ययुक्ता उपासते ॥","iast":"satataṃ kīrtayanto māṃ yatantaśca dṛḍhavratāḥ |\nnamasyantaśca māṃ bhaktyā nityayuktā upāsate ||","read":"satatam keertayanto maam yatantashcha dridhavrataah |\nnamasyantashcha maam bhaktyaa nityayuktaa upaasate ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"Always magnifying Me, strenuous, firm in vows, prostrating themselves before Me, they worship Me with devotion ever harmonised.","en2":"Glorifying Me always and striving with firm resolve, bowing down to Me in devotion, always steadfast, they worship Me.","en2r":null,"rv":null,"kid":"Krishna says these people are always praising him and trying hard, firm in what they have promised. They bow down to him with devotion and worship him, always steady."},{"v":15,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"ज्ञानयज्ञेन चाप्यन्ये यजन्तो मामुपासते ।\nएकत्वेन पृथक्त्वेन बहुधा विश्वतोमुखम् ॥","iast":"jñānayajñena cāpyanye yajanto māmupāsate |\nekatvena pṛthaktvena bahudhā viśvatomukham ||","read":"jnaanayajnena chaapyanye yajanto maamupaasate |\nekatvena prithaktvena bahudhaa vishvatomukham ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"Others also, sacrificing with the sacrifice of wisdom, worship Me as the One and the Manifold everywhere present.","en2":"Others, too, sacrificing by the Yajna of knowledge ( i.e. , seeing the Self in all), worship Me the All-Formed, as one, as distinct, as manifold.","en2r":null,"rv":null,"kid":"Krishna says that others worship him by offering wisdom. They see him as the One and as the many, present everywhere."},{"v":16,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"अहं क्रतुरहं यज्ञः स्वधाऽहमहमौषधम् ।\nमंत्रोऽहमहमेवाज्यमहमग्निरहं हुतम् ॥","iast":"ahaṃ kraturahaṃ yajñaḥ svadhā’hamahamauṣadham |\nmaṃtro’hamahamevājyamahamagnirahaṃ hutam ||","read":"aham kraturaham yajnah svadhaa'hamahamaushadham |\nmamtro'hamahamevaajyamahamagniraham hutam ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"I the ablation; I the sacrifice; I the ancestral offering; I the fire-giving herb; the mantram I; I also the butter; I the fire; the burnt-offering I;","en2":"I am the Kratu, I the Yajna, I the Svadhâ, I the Aushadham, I the Mantra, I the Ajyam, I the fire, and I the oblation.","en2r":null,"rv":null,"kid":"Krishna says that he is every part of the holy offering: the rite, the offering to the ancestors, the herb, the sacred words, the butter, the fire and the offering itself."},{"v":17,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"पिताऽहमस्य जगतो माता धाता पितामहः ।\nवेद्यं पवित्रमोंकार ऋक् साम यजुरेव च ॥","iast":"pitā’hamasya jagato mātā dhātā pitāmahaḥ |\nvedyaṃ pavitramoṃkāra ṛk sāma yajureva ca ||","read":"pitaa'hamasya jagato maataa dhaataa pitaamahah |\nvedyam pavitramomkaara rik saama yajureva cha ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"I the Father of this universe, the Mother, the Supporter, the Grandsire, the Holy one to be known, the Word of Power, and also the Rik, Sâma, and Yajur,","en2":"I am the Father of this world, the Mother, the Sustainer, the Grandfather; the Purifier, the (one) thing to be known, (the syllable) Om, and also the Rik, Sâman and Yajus.","en2r":null,"rv":null,"kid":"Krishna says he is the father and the mother of this world, its supporter and its grandfather. He is the holy one to be known, the sacred word, and the old sacred hymns."},{"v":18,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"गतिर्भर्ता प्रभुः साक्षी निवासः शरणं सुहृत् ।\nप्रभवः प्रलयः स्थानं निधानं बीजमव्ययम् ॥","iast":"gatirbhartā prabhuḥ sākṣī nivāsaḥ śaraṇaṃ suhṛt |\nprabhavaḥ pralayaḥ sthānaṃ nidhānaṃ bījamavyayam ||","read":"gatirbhartaa prabhuh saakshee nivaasah sharanam suhrit |\nprabhavah pralayah sthaanam nidhaanam beejamavyayam ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"The Path, Husband, Lord, Witness, Abode, Shelter, Lover, Origin, Dissolution, Foundation, house, Seed imperishable.","en2":"The Goal, the Supporter, the Lord, the Witness, the Abode, the Refuge, the Friend, the Origin, the Dissolution, the Substratum, the Storehouse, the Seed immutable.","en2r":null,"rv":null,"kid":"Krishna goes on. He is the way and the goal, the lord, the witness, the home, the shelter, the dear one, the beginning and the ending, the ground, the storehouse, and the seed that never dies."},{"v":19,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"तपाम्यहमहं वर्षं निगृह्णाम्युत्सृजामि च ।\nअमृतं चैव मृत्युश्च सदसच्चाहमर्जुन ॥","iast":"tapāmyahamahaṃ varṣaṃ nigṛhṇāmyutsṛjāmi ca |\namṛtaṃ caiva mṛtyuśca sadasaccāhamarjuna ||","read":"tapaamyahamaham varsham nigrihnaamyutsrijaami cha |\namritam chaiva mrityushcha sadasachchaahamarjuna ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"I give heat; I hold back and send forth the rain; immortality and also death, being and non-being am I, Arjuna.","en2":"(As sun) I give heat: I withhold and send forth rain; I am immortality and also death; being and non-being am I, O Arjuna!","en2r":null,"rv":null,"kid":"Krishna tells Arjuna that he gives heat, and he holds back and sends forth the rain. He is deathlessness and also death. He is what is and what is not."},{"v":20,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"त्रैविद्या मां सोमपाः पूतपापा ।\nयज्ञैरिष्ट्वा स्वर्गतिं प्रार्थयन्ते ।\nते पुण्यमासाद्य सुरेन्द्रलोक ।\nमश्नन्ति दिव्यान्दिवि देवभोगान् ॥","iast":"traividyā māṃ somapāḥ pūtapāpā |\nyajñairiṣṭvā svargatiṃ prārthayante |\nte puṇyamāsādya surendraloka |\nmaśnanti divyāndivi devabhogān ||","read":"traividyaa maam somapaah pootapaapaa |\nyajnairishtvaa svargatim praarthayante |\nte punyamaasaadya surendraloka |\nmashnanti divyaandivi devabhogaan ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"The knowers of the three, the Soma-drinkers, the purified from sin, worshipping Me with sacrifice, pray of Me the way to heaven; they, ascending to the holy world of the Ruler of the Shining Ones, eat in heaven the divine feasts of the Shining Ones.","en2":"The knowers of the three Vedas, worshipping Me by Yajna, drinking the Soma, and (thus) being purified from sin, pray for passage to heaven; reaching the holy world of the Lord of the Devas, they enjoy in heaven the divine pleasures of the Devas.","en2r":null,"rv":null,"kid":"Krishna says some who know the three Vedas worship him with offerings, are made clean of wrong, and pray to reach heaven. They reach the holy world of the ruler of the Shining Ones and enjoy its divine joys."},{"v":21,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"ते तं भुक्त्वा स्वर्गलोकं विशालं ।\nक्षीणे पुण्ये मर्त्यलोकं विशन्ति ।\nएवं त्रयीधर्ममनुप्रपन्ना ।\nगतागतं कामकामा लभन्ते ॥","iast":"te taṃ bhuktvā svargalokaṃ viśālaṃ |\nkṣīṇe puṇye martyalokaṃ viśanti |\nevaṃ trayīdharmamanuprapannā |\ngatāgataṃ kāmakāmā labhante ||","read":"te tam bhuktvaa svargalokam vishaalam |\nksheene punye martyalokam vishanti |\nevam trayeedharmamanuprapannaa |\ngataagatam kaamakaamaa labhante ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"They, having enjoyed the spacious heaven-world, their holiness withered, come back to this world of death. Following the virtues enjoined by the three, desiring desires, they obtain the transitory.","en2":"Having enjoyed the vast Swarga-world, they enter the mortal world, on the exhaustion of their merit: Thus, abiding by the injunctions of the three (Vedas), desiring desires, they (constantly) come and go.","en2r":null,"rv":null,"kid":"Krishna says that when they have enjoyed the wide heaven-world and their goodness is used up, they come back to this world of death. Because they want what they desire, they keep coming and going."},{"v":22,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"अनन्याश्चिन्तयन्तो मां ये जनाः पर्युपासते ।\nतेषां नित्याभियुक्तानां योगक्षेमं वहाम्यहम् ॥","iast":"ananyāścintayanto māṃ ye janāḥ paryupāsate |\nteṣāṃ nityābhiyuktānāṃ yogakṣemaṃ vahāmyaham ||","read":"ananyaashchintayanto maam ye janaah paryupaasate |\nteshaam nityaabhiyuktaanaam yogakshemam vahaamyaham ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"To those men who worship Me alone thinking of no other, to those ever harmonious, I bring full security.","en2":"Persons who, meditating on Me as non-separate, worship Me in all beings, to them thus ever jealously engaged, I carry what they lack and preserve what they already have.","en2r":null,"rv":null,"kid":"Krishna says that he takes full care of those who worship him alone, thinking of nothing apart from him, and who stay always steady."},{"v":23,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"येऽप्यन्यदेवता भक्ता यजन्ते श्रद्धयाऽन्विताः ।\nतेऽपि मामेव कौन्तेय यजन्त्यविधिपूर्वकम् ॥","iast":"ye’pyanyadevatā bhaktā yajante śraddhayā’nvitāḥ |\nte’pi māmeva kaunteya yajantyavidhipūrvakam ||","read":"ye'pyanyadevataa bhaktaa yajante shraddhayaa'nvitaah |\nte'pi maameva kaunteya yajantyavidhipoorvakam ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"Even the devotees of other Shining Ones, who worship full of faith, they also worship Me, O son of Kuntî, though contrary to the ancient rule.","en2":"Even those devotees, who endued with Shraddhâ, worship other gods, they too worship Me alone, O son of Kunti, (but) by the wrong method.","en2r":null,"rv":null,"kid":"Krishna tells Arjuna that people who worship other Shining Ones with faith are worshipping him too, even though they do not follow the old rule."},{"v":24,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"अहं हि सर्वयज्ञानां भोक्ता च प्रभुरेव च ।\nन तु मामभिजानन्ति तत्त्वेनातश्च्यवन्ति ते ॥","iast":"ahaṃ hi sarvayajñānāṃ bhoktā ca prabhureva ca |\nna tu māmabhijānanti tattvenātaścyavanti te ||","read":"aham hi sarvayajnaanaam bhoktaa cha prabhureva cha |\nna tu maamabhijaananti tattvenaatashchyavanti te ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"I am indeed the enjoyer of all sacrifices and also the Lord, but they know Me not in Essence, and hence they fall.","en2":"For I alone am the Enjoyer, and Lord of all Yajnas; but because they do not know Me in reality, they return, (to the mortal world).","en2r":null,"rv":null,"kid":"Krishna says that he is the one who receives every offering, and he is its Lord. But these people do not truly know him, and so they fall back."},{"v":25,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"यान्ति देवव्रता देवान् पितॄन्यान्ति पितृव्रताः ।\nभूतानि यान्ति भूतेज्या यान्ति मद्याजिनोऽपि माम् ॥","iast":"yānti devavratā devān pitṝnyānti pitṛvratāḥ |\nbhūtāni yānti bhūtejyā yānti madyājino’pi mām ||","read":"yaanti devavrataa devaan pitreenyaanti pitrivrataah |\nbhootaani yaanti bhootejyaa yaanti madyaajino'pi maam ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"They who worship the Shining Ones go to the Shining Ones; to the Ancestors go the Ancestor-worshippers; to the Elements go those who sacrifice to Elementals; but My worshippers come unto Me.","en2":"Votaries of the Devas go to the Devas; to the Pitris, go their votaries; to the Bhutas, go the Bhuta worshippers; My votaries too come unto Me.","en2r":null,"rv":null,"kid":"Krishna says that those who worship the Shining Ones go to them, those who worship the ancestors go to the ancestors, and those who offer to the elements go to the elements. Those who worship him come to him."},{"v":26,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"पत्रं पुष्पं फलं तोयं यो मे भक्त्या प्रयच्छति ।\nतदहं भक्त्युपहृतमश्नामि प्रयतात्मनः ॥","iast":"patraṃ puṣpaṃ phalaṃ toyaṃ yo me bhaktyā prayacchati |\ntadahaṃ bhaktyupahṛtamaśnāmi prayatātmanaḥ ||","read":"patram pushpam phalam toyam yo me bhaktyaa prayachchhati |\ntadaham bhaktyupahritamashnaami prayataatmanah ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"He who offereth to Me with devotion a leaf, a flower, a fruit, water, that I accept from the striving self, offered as it is with devotion.","en2":"Whoever with devotion offers Me a leaf, a flower, a fruit, or water, that I accept—the devout gift of the pure-minded.","en2r":null,"rv":null,"kid":"Krishna says that if someone offers him a leaf, a flower, a fruit or some water with devotion, he accepts that gift, given with devotion."},{"v":27,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"यत्करोषि यदश्नासि यज्जुहोषि ददासि यत् ।\nयत्तपस्यसि कौन्तेय तत्कुरुष्व मदर्पणम् ॥","iast":"yatkaroṣi yadaśnāsi yajjuhoṣi dadāsi yat |\nyattapasyasi kaunteya tatkuruṣva madarpaṇam ||","read":"yatkaroshi yadashnaasi yajjuhoshi dadaasi yat |\nyattapasyasi kaunteya tatkurushva madarpanam ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"Whatsoever thou doest, whatsoever thou eatest, whatsoever thou offerest, whatsoever thou givest, whatsoever thou doest of austerity, O Kaunteya, do thou that as an offering unto Me.","en2":"Whatever thou doest, whatever thou eatest, whatever thou offerest in sacrifice, whatever thou givest away, whatever austerity thou practisest, O son of Kunti, do that as an offering unto Me.","en2r":null,"rv":null,"kid":"Krishna tells Arjuna that whatever he does, whatever he eats, whatever he offers, whatever he gives away and whatever hard practice he keeps, he should do it all as an offering to Krishna."},{"v":28,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"शुभाशुभफलैरेवं मोक्ष्यसे कर्मबन्धनैः ।\nसंन्यासयोगयुक्तात्मा विमुक्तो मामुपैष्यसि ॥","iast":"śubhāśubhaphalairevaṃ mokṣyase karmabandhanaiḥ |\nsaṃnyāsayogayuktātmā vimukto māmupaiṣyasi ||","read":"shubhaashubhaphalairevam mokshyase karmabandhanaih |\nsamnyaasayogayuktaatmaa vimukto maamupaishyasi ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"Thus shalt thou be liberated from the bonds of action, yielding good and evil fruits; thyself harmonised by the yoga of renunciation, thou shalt come unto Me when set free.","en2":"Thus shalt thou be freed from the bondages of actions, bearing good and evil results: with the heart steadfast in the Yoga of renunciation, and liberated, thou shalt come unto Me.","en2r":null,"rv":null,"kid":"Krishna says that in this way Arjuna will be freed from the bonds of action, with their good and bad results. His heart steady in letting go, he will be free and come to Krishna."},{"v":29,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"समोऽहं सर्वभूतेषु न मे द्वेष्योऽस्ति न प्रियः ।\nये भजन्ति तु मां भक्त्या मयि ते तेषु चाप्यहम् ॥","iast":"samo’haṃ sarvabhūteṣu na me dveṣyo’sti na priyaḥ |\nye bhajanti tu māṃ bhaktyā mayi te teṣu cāpyaham ||","read":"samo'ham sarvabhooteshu na me dveshyo'sti na priyah |\nye bhajanti tu maam bhaktyaa mayi te teshu chaapyaham ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"The same am I to all beings; there is none hateful to Me nor dear. They verily who worship Me with devotion, they are in Me, and I also in them.","en2":"I am the same to all beings: to Me there is none hateful or dear. But those who worship Me with devotion, are in Me, and I too am in them.","en2r":null,"rv":null,"kid":"Krishna says he is the same to all beings. He hates no one, and no one is his favourite. But those who worship him with devotion are in him, and he is in them."},{"v":30,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"अपि चेत्सुदुराचारो भजते मामनन्यभाक् ।\nसाधुरेव स मन्तव्यः सम्यग्व्यवसितो हि सः ॥","iast":"api cetsudurācāro bhajate māmananyabhāk |\nsādhureva sa mantavyaḥ samyagvyavasito hi saḥ ||","read":"api chetsuduraachaaro bhajate maamananyabhaak |\nsaadhureva sa mantavyah samyagvyavasito hi sah ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"Even if the most sinful worship Me, with un divided heart, he too must be accounted righteous, for he hath rightly resolved;","en2":"If even a very wicked person worships Me, with devotion to none else, he should be regarded as good, for he has rightly resolved.","en2r":null,"rv":null,"kid":"Krishna says that even if a very wicked person worships him with a whole heart, turning to no one else, that person should be thought of as good, because they have chosen rightly."},{"v":31,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"क्षिप्रं भवति धर्मात्मा शश्वच्छान्तिं निगच्छति ।\nकौन्तेय प्रतिजानीहि न मे भक्तः प्रणश्यति ॥","iast":"kṣipraṃ bhavati dharmātmā śaśvacchāntiṃ nigacchati |\nkaunteya pratijānīhi na me bhaktaḥ praṇaśyati ||","read":"kshipram bhavati dharmaatmaa shashvachchhaantim nigachchhati |\nkaunteya pratijaaneehi na me bhaktah pranashyati ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"Speedily he becometh dutiful and goeth to eternal peace; O Kaunteya, know thou for certain that My devotee perisheth never.","en2":"Soon does he become righteous, and attain eternal Peace, O son of Kunti boldly canst thou proclaim, that My devotee is never destroyed.","en2r":null,"rv":null,"kid":"Krishna says such a person soon becomes good and reaches lasting peace. He tells Arjuna to know for certain that one who is devoted to him is never destroyed."},{"v":32,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"मां हि पार्थ व्यपाश्रित्य येऽपि स्युः पापयोनयः ।\nस्त्रियो वैश्यास्तथा शूद्रास्तेऽपि यान्ति परां गतिम् ॥","iast":"māṃ hi pārtha vyapāśritya ye’pi syuḥ pāpayonayaḥ |\nstriyo vaiśyāstathā śūdrāste’pi yānti parāṃ gatim ||","read":"maam hi paartha vyapaashritya ye'pi syuh paapayonayah |\nstriyo vaishyaastathaa shoodraaste'pi yaanti paraam gatim ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"They who take refuge with Me, O Partha, though of the womb of sin, women, Vaishyas, even Shûdras, they also tread the highest path.","en2":"For, taking refuge in Me, they also, O son of Prithâ, who might be of inferior birth,—women, Vaishyas, as well as Sudras,—even they attain to the Supreme Goal.","en2r":null,"rv":null,"kid":"Krishna tells Arjuna that those who take shelter in him reach the highest goal too, whatever birth they come from."},{"v":33,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"किं पुनर्ब्राह्मणाः पुण्या भक्ता राजर्षयस्तथा ।\nअनित्यमसुखं लोकमिमं प्राप्य भजस्व माम् ॥","iast":"kiṃ punarbrāhmaṇāḥ puṇyā bhaktā rājarṣayastathā |\nanityamasukhaṃ lokamimaṃ prāpya bhajasva mām ||","read":"kim punarbraahmanaah punyaa bhaktaa raajarshayastathaa |\nanityamasukham lokamimam praapya bhajasva maam ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"How much rather then holy Brâhmanas and devoted royal saints; having obtained this transient joyless world, worship thou Me.","en2":"What need to mention holy Brâhmanas, and devoted Râjarshis! Having obtained this transient, joyless world, worship thou Me.","en2r":null,"rv":null,"kid":"Krishna says this is even more true of holy people and devoted royal sages. He tells Arjuna that, having come into this passing and joyless world, he should worship Krishna."},{"v":34,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"मन्मना भव मद्भक्तो मद्याजी मां नमस्कुरु ।\nमामेवैष्यसि युक्त्वैवमात्मानं मत्परायणः ॥","iast":"manmanā bhava madbhakto madyājī māṃ namaskuru |\nmāmevaiṣyasi yuktvaivamātmānaṃ matparāyaṇaḥ ||","read":"manmanaa bhava madbhakto madyaajee maam namaskuru |\nmaamevaishyasi yuktvaivamaatmaanam matparaayanah ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"On Me fix thy mind, be devoted to Me; sacrifice to Me; prostrate thyself before Me; harmonised thus in the Self, thou shalt come unto Me, having Me as thy supreme goal.","en2":"Fill thy mind with Me, be My devotee, sacrifice unto Me, bow down to Me; thus having made thy heart steadfast in Me, taking Me as the Supreme Goal, thou shalt come to Me.","en2r":null,"rv":null,"kid":"Krishna tells Arjuna to fill his mind with him, be devoted to him, offer to him and bow to him. With his heart steady like this, and Krishna as his highest goal, he will come to Krishna."}];
